A||||4||fierogt88||StuGood = do good!!||||7||
Z||000000||fierogt88||01-30-2001||10:22 AM||||I would like to take a moment to thank StuGood.  I mentioned in one of my posts that I had snapped my gt emblem on the front fascia off while waxing my car, and StuGood sent me the piece to repair it asking nothing in return.  He's a real stand-up guy and I suggest that if he ever finds himself in need of anything that everyone shows him the same good-will that he showed me.<P>The comeraderie of fiero owners is probably the most satisfying part of owning one.  When I bought my GT last september it had the TCC lockup problem and when I stalled it trying to pull into a McDonald's parking lot TWO people jumped out of their cars and helped me push it into the lot.  Not only that but they turned out to be fellow fiero owners and we sat there and chatted.  My wife was NOT happy about traveling 300 miles and paying 5000 dollars for a car that had problems, but these people were so impressed with the car that my wife stopped crying and let me keep it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>So, if anybody else has stories of how they were impressed by the friendliness of fiero owners, or want to thank anybody, feel free to do it under this topic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000001||fropuff||01-30-2001||03:30 PM||||There's only been a few people that have sent me stuff, such as 87ECO5, who sent me a free ash tray cover, and Fierodave, who gave me a free shift knob when we traded some stuff.  I know that there's many others that do good things like that, but I haven't done any business with them.  Thanks a lot, everyone, who makes the Fiero parts business such a good time!  Also, I would like to thank everyone that has helped me out since I joined last year.  There's been a lot of you, and I really appreciate the help, no matter if the information you give me is a large or small amount.  I know that I can be an annoying little piece of crap with my repetitive questions, but I really appreciate the people that can tolerate them.  THANKS A LOT EVERYONE!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||01-30-2001||06:58 PM||||Well, Iv never needed anything like that, but if someone wants to donate a 3.4 engine to me that would be great!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> StuGood is a very helpful person (in detecting tach filter problems, sorry couldn't help myself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) There are some great memebers here that a willing to help out others without question. There are a few folks here I have done business with, like mrfiero in colorado, and Rodney Dickman. Both great people to deal with and Iv never had a problem. Myself and Others I know are getting very concerned with our Ground-Control Coil-over order from Mike. I havent recieved any word in over a month about whats going on. I know some folks here have done business with him, and he does have a good reputation. But, unless he's in lieing on a hosptital bed sick to death, I cant understand why he wont respond?!?||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||01-31-2001||12:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierogt88:<BR><B>...StuGood sent me the piece...He's a real stand-up guy...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>...maybe a stand-up comedian, anyway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  Glad you got the part - and you didn't even make fun of my wrapping job!  I had no plans for the part myself, it's one less thing in my garage, and you had use for it.  Everybody wins.   Thanks for the kind words  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
